25,2,1,talk,Servas,,"It appears we have a surplus of coders, but our phenotyping technicians have vanished. However, the glasshouse crew is surprisingly intact.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Sakura,,"Shipping costs are eating the budget, but the ministry is still paying for glasshouse bench fees! Also, computing hours are now free.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Daisuke,,"Catalogues have lasting value, but mechanism studies often fail. Also, breeding colonies are far more likely to cause delays than computers.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Takumi,,"Field sites are a disaster zone with floods and fires. Worse, the spectroscopy suite was down for eleven weeks!","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Minako,,"The animal facility is finally accredited with vet cover, but the glasshouses are completely booked up. On the bright side, repository deposits are now very fast.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Sakura, if computing is free and the glasshouse crew is strong, those are our safest bets.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Sakura,,"Exactly, Servas! But @Minako, if the glasshouses are booked solid, can we even start a plant project?","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Servas"",""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Daisuke,,I am worried about any project relying on breeding colonies... the overruns are too frequent.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Takumi,,"@Minako, is the repository speed enough to offset the fact that field sites are burning down or flooding?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Sakura, the booking situation is tight, but the infrastructure is there. @Takumi, the repository is a huge win for data-heavy projects.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Sakura"",""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,3,talk,Servas,,"@Daisuke, your finding about catalogues is interesting. They seem to be the most stable investment.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Daisuke""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,3,talk,Sakura,,"@Takumi, if spectroscopy is unreliable, we should definitely avoid any project that depends on it for timing.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,3,talk,Daisuke,,I agree. I would feel much safer with a project that aggregates data rather than one chasing a single elusive mechanism.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,3,talk,Takumi,,"I'm with Sakura. If the equipment is broken and the field sites are gone, we need something indoor and digital.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[""Sakura""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,3,talk,Minako,,"It seems we need a balance: something that uses the available staff and the fast repository, but avoids the animal and spectroscopy risks.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
