50,3,1,talk,Servas,,"The candidates are A: Microbiome Atlas, B: Protein Folding, C: Amphibian Regeneration, and D: Plant Drought Signaling. I lean toward A.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,3,1,talk,Sakura,,A looks great because it uses the repository and doesn't need the expensive shipping or animal rates!,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,3,1,talk,Daisuke,,"A is a catalogue project. Based on the closeout files, it is the most likely to actually deliver lasting results.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,3,1,talk,Takumi,,B needs spectroscopy and C needs breeding colonies. Both are huge red flags. A avoids the field site disasters too.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,3,1,talk,Minako,,"D is tempting because of the glasshouse crew, but the blocks are booked solid. A is the most operationally feasible.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,2,talk,Servas,,"@Minako, do you think the booking backlog for D is a dealbreaker?","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,2,talk,Sakura,,"I do! Plus, A takes advantage of the free computing hours I found.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,2,talk,Daisuke,,"@Takumi, do you think the Atlas is resilient enough if one of its climate zones has a field failure?","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[""Takumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,2,talk,Takumi,,"Yes, because it's a collection. One site failing won't kill the whole atlas, unlike a specific breeding colony.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Servas, yes, the booking situation for D is too risky. A is the cleanest path forward.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,3,talk,Servas,,I am convinced. A utilizes our available coders and the improved repository turnaround.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,3,talk,Sakura,,I'm voting for A! It's the most exciting and safest choice.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,3,talk,Daisuke,,I agree. A is the most rational choice for long-term success.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,3,talk,Takumi,,"A it is. No broken machines, no flooded sites.","{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,3,talk,Minako,,I concur. A is the most stable option.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,4,talk,Servas,,Then we are in harmony. I vote for A.,"{""words"":9,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
